quadratic probing want to solve cluster problem in linear probing
he search for free indexes by x^2 steps, so the items will not insert side by side like linear probing
but he can miss some free indexes and trapped in infinite loop!
(in linear probing we check all the array, so we don't miss anythings)

in linear probing, when we have a collision
we just check the next index ( newIndex = (h(k) + i) % m)
but in quadratic probing
nextIndex = (h(k) + i^2) % m

imagine our hash table use a Array with length of 10
and we use quadratic probing for resolve the collisions
(our hash function is h(k) = k % m)
[,,,,,,,,,]


insert 23 (k = 23)
                 h(23) = 23 % 10 = 3
                 [,,,23,,,,,,]

insert 33 (k = 33)
                 h(33) = 33 % 10 = 3
                 the index of 3 is full!
                 newIndex = (h(k) + i^2) % m        set i =1
                          = (3    + 1^2) % 10
                          = 4
                 [,,,23,33,,,,,]

insert 42 (k = 42)
                 h(42) = 42 % 10 = 2
                 [,,42,23,33,,,,,]

insert 43 (k =43)
                 h(43) = 43 % 10 =3
                 the index of 3 is full!
                 newIndex = (h(k) + i^2) % m        set i=1
                          = (3    + 1^2) % 10
                          = 4
                 the index of 4 is full!            set i=2
                 newIndex = (3    + 2^2) % 10
                          = 7
                 [,,42,23,33,,,43,,]


insert 53 (k = 53)
                 h(43) = 43 % 10 =3
                 the index of 3 is full!
                 newIndex = (h(k) + i^2) % m        set i=1
                          = (3    + 1^2) % 10
                          = 4
                 the index of 4 is full!
                 newIndex = (3    + 2^2) % 10       set i=2
                          = 7
                 the index of 7 is full!
